  },
  {
   "id": "F-SEC-2",
   "severity": "low",
   "text": "Receipt upload validates the file EXTENSION only: a plain-text file named .png was accepted (201). Receipts are stored privately and served through an authenticated download, which bounds the impact. Decision: add magic-byte content sniffing at upload (receipts + avatars share the pattern)."
  },
  {
   "id": "F-SEC-3",
   "severity": "low (production gate)",
   "text": "Session cookie is HttpOnly + SameSite=Strict but has no Secure flag in the dev configuration (expected on http://localhost). The sign-in code clones env.COOKIE_OPTIONS, so production must set Secure via environment - fold into the existing production TLS/secrets gate checklist."
  },
  {
   "id": "F-SEC-4",
   "severity": "info",
   "text": "A CORS preflight from a disallowed origin returns HTTP 500 instead of a clean denial response. Browsers still block the request; optional middleware polish to return 403/no-ACAO."
  },
  {
   "id": "F-SEC-5",
   "severity": "info",
   "text": "Deleting a user leaves orphaned AgencyMembership rows (observed once during this review; the orphan was removed by exact ID). Inert (the user cannot authenticate), but a cascade or cleanup job is tidier. Decision: cascade memberships on user deletion or leave as documented behavior."
  },
  {
   "id": "F-SEC-6",
   "severity": "info",
   "text": "Local-dev Mongo credentials appear in tracked files (compose files, the P0 script, two roadmap lines). They protect only the loopback dev stack; production credentials must be different and secret-managed (existing production gate). Optional: scrub the two roadmap lines."
  },
  {
   "id": "F-SEC-7",
   "severity": "info",
   "text": "Sign-in does not enforce the user.verified flag (email activation is advisory in this build): an admin-created unverified supplier could sign in during this review. That is the intended admin-onboarding flow; for self-signup it means verification is not a sign-in barrier. Product decision if that should change."
  }
